ement: replace all occurrences of old with new\n        # But careful: we need to apply replacement once per pass, not repeatedly.\n        # Python str.replace(old, new) replaces all non-overlapping occurrences.\n        new_text = text.replace(old, new)\n        if new_text != text:\n            text = new_text\n            applications.append(pass_[\"name\"])\n            changed_this_round = True\n    if not changed_this_round:\n        fixed_point = True\n        break\nelse:\n    # loop completed without break => max_rounds exhausted, not fixed point\n    fixed_point = False\n\nReturn {\"applications\": applications, \"fixed_point\": fixed_point, \"text\": text}\n\nIs that correct? Need to consider potential overlapping replacements? Python replace handles non-overlapping left-to-right. That's fine.\n\nAlso note: Passes might be applied multiple times in same round? For example, after applying halve-a, the new text might create new occurrences for drop-b? But the order within round is fixed. So in each round we iterate in order and apply each pass exactly once. That's correct.\n\nPotential nuance: In each round, do we apply all passes regardless of changes? Yes. But we record only when change occurs.\n\nNow we must produce the output as a JSON object with key \"implementation\". The value is a string containing the Python source. Must be valid JSON, so escape quotes and newlines.\n\nWe'll write the solve function with proper indentation.\n\nAlso note: The task says \"may use only the Python standard library\". So no imports needed beyond possibly typing but not required.\n\nEdge: Ensure we handle case where pass names might not be unique? Probably unique but not guaranteed. Use as given.\n\nNow produce the response.\n\nBut note: The user provided a long message with \"STRICT SUBMISSION ENVELOPE\" etc. The final answer must be only one JSON object with key \"implementation\". Do not include any other text.\n\nWe'll produce:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(c